  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-03-11T14:56:31.491Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As of build 1061 the SyncVideoStream player appears to be having intermittent issues with syncing players, the issue appears to be worse in SDK2 worlds, SDK3 worlds are better, but still intermittently won't sync for some users.\nI run a weekly event, last week on build 1058 I encountered no issues with sync, the event went well, this week usually a quarter of the lobby would either be stuck with the last frame of the video file or a blank screen.\nI tested this in a couple worlds, one being my own world that uses a basic SyncVideoStream component and does not utilize the AVPro packages, and Kareedas public world which I don't know if it uses AVPro components, both exhibited the same sync issues.\nForcing a resync might fix one user, but another would break, instance master would always display the video just fine, only non master players are effected.\nIn SDK3/Udon worlds sync would be better, but some users would have to rejoin the instance to get sync to start, and one user even after that still couldn't start it.\nThese issues were experienced with a lobby size around 15-20 users.",
